 "創作": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]\nمثال: この画家は美しい絵画を創作する。\n→ This artist creates beautiful paintings. / فَبْرَكَة (That which is fabricated; a falsehood.)  [fabrication]\nمثال: それは彼女の創作だろう。\n→ I think she made up that story.",
 "創作力": "عَبْقَرِيّ, نَابِغَة (Someone possessing extraordinary intelligence or skill; especially somebody who ) / عَبْقَرِيَّة (Extraordinary mental capacity.) / عَبْقَرِيّ (Ingenious, brilliant, very clever, or original.)  [genius]",
 "創作的": "إِبْداعِيّ, خَلَّاق (Tending to create things, or having the ability to create; often, excellently, i)  [creative]",
 "創作者": "خَالِق (The deity that created the world.) / مُبْدِع (A player who creates opportunities for their team to score goals; a playmaker.)  [creator]",
 "創傷": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [wound]",
 "創出": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]\nمثال: ここでの問題は、社会のトレンドを概観できるような枠組みを創出することである。\n→ The question here is one of creating the framework with which we can outline the social trend.",
 "創刊": "إِنْشاء, إِشَادَة (The act of founding, fixing, establishing, or beginning to erect.) / أَسَاس, قَاعِدَة (That upon which anything is founded; that on which anything stands, and by which) / مُؤَسَّسَة (That which is founded, or established by endowment; an endowed institution or ch) / أَسَاس (Cosmetic cream roughly skin-colored, designed to make the face appear uniform in)  [foundation (of a newspaper, magazine, etc.)]\nمثال: 日本創刊を果たしたイギリス発のホームレスの人だけが販売者となれるストリートペーパー「ビッグイシュー」について紹介しよう。\n→ I shall be introducing the street paper that is only sold by the homeless, \"The Big Issue\", started in England and has had its first…",
 "創始": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]",
 "創始者": "مُؤَسِّس, مُؤَسِّسَة (One who founds or establishes (a company, project, organisation, state, etc.).)  [founder]",
 "創始者効果": "تَأْثِير المُؤَسِّس, تَأْثِير المُؤَسَّسَة (A reduction in genetic diversity resulting when a population is descended from a)  [founder effect]",
 "創建": "تَأْسِيس (The act or process of establishing; a ratifying or ordaining; settlement; confir) / تَأْسِيس (The state of being established, founded, etc.; fixed state.) / مُؤَسَّسَة (That which is established; as a form of government, a permanent organization, bu)  [establishment]\nمثال: 城の創建は１１世紀にさかのぼると伝えられる。\n→ It is said that the castle dates back to the 11th century.",
 "創建者": "مُؤَسِّس, مُؤَسِّسَة (One who founds or establishes (a company, project, organisation, state, etc.).)  [founder]",
 "創成": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]",
 "創案": "حَبِلَ (To have a child; to become pregnant (with).) / خَرَجَ بِ (To develop; to form in the mind; to imagine.)  [conceiving (an idea)]",
