 "創見": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]",
 "創設": "تَأْسِيس (The act or process of establishing; a ratifying or ordaining; settlement; confir) / تَأْسِيس (The state of being established, founded, etc.; fixed state.) / مُؤَسَّسَة (That which is established; as a form of government, a permanent organization, bu)  [establishment]\nمثال: 彼らは新しい会社を創設するつもりだ。\n→ They will set up a new company.",
 "創設者": "مُؤَسِّس, مُؤَسِّسَة (One who founds or establishes (a company, project, organisation, state, etc.).)  [founder]",
 "創造": "خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [creation]\nمثال: 神は自分の形に人を創造された。\n→ God created man in his own image. / خِلْقَة, خَلْق (Something created such as an invention or artwork.) / اِبْتِكَار, خَلْق (The act of creating something.) / خَلْق (All which exists.)  [Creation (by God)]",
 "創造主": "خَالِق (The deity that created the world.) / مُبْدِع (A player who creates opportunities for their team to score goals; a playmaker.)  [Creator]",
 "創造力": "إِبْدَاع (The ability to use imagination to produce a novel idea or product.)  [creativity]\nمثال: テレビは創造力を鈍らせる力がある。\n→ Television can dull our creative power.",
 "創造性": "إِبْدَاع (The ability to use imagination to produce a novel idea or product.)  [creativity]\nمثال: その影響力は日毎にますます大きくなっているが、しかし創造性があるわけではなく、また、価値の判断もできない。\n→ Their influence becomes greater every day, but they are uncreative and can't make value judgements.",
 "創造物": "مَخْلُوق, كَائِن (A living being, such as an animal, monster, or alien.)  [creature]\nمثال: 科学的心理は人間精神の創造物である。\n→ Scientific truth is a creation of the human mind.",
 "創造的": "إِبْداعِيّ, خَلَّاق (Tending to create things, or having the ability to create; often, excellently, i)  [creative]\nمثال: 彼は創造的精神が欠けている。\n→ He is barren of creative spirit.",
 "創造者": "خَالِق (The deity that created the world.) / مُبْدِع (A player who creates opportunities for their team to score goals; a playmaker.)  [creator]\nمثال: 神は創造者です。天も地も人も、神以外は全て被造物です。\n→ God is the creator. Heaven and Earth and people and everything apart from God are created.",
 "剽げる": "طُرْفَة, نُكْتَة (An amusing story.) / نُكْتَة, هَزْل (Something said or done for amusement, not in seriousness.) / مَزَحَ (To dupe in a friendly manner for amusement; to mess with, play with.)  [to joke]",
 "剽悍": "جَرِيء, جَسُور (Adventurous, willing to take on or look for risks; overbold.)  [daring]",
 "剽盗": "قاطِعُ طَرِيق, قُطّاعُ ٱلطُّرُق (A person, usually mounted on horseback, who robbed travelers on public roads.)  [highwayman]",
 "剽窃": "اِنْتِحال (Copying of another person's ideas, text, or other creative work, and presenting )  [plagiarism]",
 "剽軽": "سَاخِر (Treating serious issues with (often deliberately) inappropriate humour; flippant) / طَرِيف (Pleasantly humorous; jocular.)  [facetious]",
 "剽軽る": "طُرْفَة, نُكْتَة (An amusing story.) / نُكْتَة, هَزْل (Something said or done for amusement, not in seriousness.) / مَزَحَ (To dupe in a friendly manner for amusement; to mess with, play with.)  [to joke]",
 "剽軽者": "جُوكَر (A playing card that features a picture of a joker (that is, a jester) and that m)  [joker]",
