 "劇": "دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (A composition, normally in prose, telling a story and intended to be represented) / دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (Theatrical plays in general.)  [drama]\nمثال: 劇はちょうど定刻に始まった。\n→ The play began exactly on time. / [powerful drug]\nabbr of 劇薬",
 "劇作家": "كَاتِب مَسْرَحِيّ (A writer and creator of theatrical plays.)  [playwright]\nمثال: イギリスの劇作家でシェイクスピアに匹敵する者はほかにいない。\n→ No other English dramatist rivals Shakespeare.",
 "劇場": "مَسْرَح (A place or building, consisting of a stage and seating, in which an audience gat) / مَسْرَح (Drama or performance as a profession or art form.)  [theater]\nمثال: さあ劇場に着いたぜ。\n→ Here we are at the theater.",
 "劇場版": "فِلْم (motion picture) / شَرِيط (motion picture) / فِيلْم سِينَمَائِيّ (motion picture) / تَصْوِير مُتَحَرِّك (motion picture)  [the movie]",
 "劇壇": "مَرْحَلَة (A phase.) / مُنَصَّة, مَسْرَح (A platform; a surface, generally elevated, upon which show performances or other)  [the stage]",
 "劇烈": "عُنْف, عَنْف (Physical action which causes destruction, harm, pain, or suffering.) / عُنْف (Widespread fighting.)  [violence]\nمثال: 我々の会社は激烈な競争に耐えきれなかった。\n→ Our company failed to survive against cutthroat competition.",
 "劇界": "مَرْحَلَة (A phase.) / مُنَصَّة, مَسْرَح (A platform; a surface, generally elevated, upon which show performances or other)  [the stage]",
 "劇的": "مُثِير (Creating or producing excitement.)  [exciting]\nمثال: 彼女が今の名声を得るに至ったいきさつは劇的である。\n→ The events that led up to her present fame are quite dramatic. / الْأُقْصَى, الْأَبْعَد (Of a place, the most remote, farthest or outermost.) / شَدِيد (In the greatest or highest degree; intense.) / غَيْر اِعْتِيَادِيّ (Excessive, or far beyond the norm.) / خَطِير (Drastic, or of great severity.) / مُتَطَرِّف (Of sports, difficult or dangerous; performed in a hazardous environment.) / أَخِير (Ultimate, final or last.)  [extreme]",
 "劇道": "دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (A composition, normally in prose, telling a story and intended to be represented) / دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (Theatrical plays in general.)  [drama]",
 "劈": "اِنْكَسَرَ (intransitive: to separate into (to end up in) two or more pi) / كَسَرَ (transitive: to separate into (to cause to end up in) two or ) / اِسْتِرَاحَة (rest or pause, usually from work)  [break]",
 "劈く": "اِنْكَسَرَ (intransitive: to separate into (to end up in) two or more pi) / كَسَرَ (transitive: to separate into (to cause to end up in) two or ) / اِسْتِرَاحَة (rest or pause, usually from work)  [to break]",
 "劈頭": "بِدَايَة (The act of doing that which begins anything; commencement of an action, state, o) / بِدَايَة (That which begins or originates something; the source or first cause.) / بِدَايَة (The initial portion of some extended thing.)  [beginning]",
 "劍": "سَيْف, حُسَام (A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together) / سَيَّافٌ (One of the end bars by which the lay of a hand loom is suspended.)  [sword (esp. a large, double-edged one)]\nمثال: 剣を取る者は皆剣で滅びる。\n→ All who take up the sword will perish by the sword. / حَرْبَة, سُونْكِيّ (A blade mounted to the end of a long gun, originally with a handle inserted into)  [bayonet] / [swordsmanship] / خزاقة (Any sharp-pointed missile weapon, such as an arrow.)  [dart]",
 "劒": "سَيْف, حُسَام (A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together) / سَيَّافٌ (One of the end bars by which the lay of a hand loom is suspended.)  [sword (esp. a large, double-edged one)]\nمثال: 剣を取る者は皆剣で滅びる。\n→ All who take up the sword will perish by the sword. / حَرْبَة, سُونْكِيّ (A blade mounted to the end of a long gun, originally with a handle inserted into)  [bayonet] / [swordsmanship] / خزاقة (Any sharp-pointed missile weapon, such as an arrow.)  [dart]",
 "力": "قُوَّة (Ability to influence; strength or energy of body or mind; active power; vigour; ) / قُوَّة (Anything that is able to make a substantial change in a person or thing.) / أَجْبَرَ, اِضْطَرَّ (To compel (an adversary or partner) to trump a trick by leading a suit that he/s)  [force]\nمثال: あなたは私の２倍の力がある。\n→ You are twice as strong as I. / قُدْرَة, مَقْدِرَة (The quality or state of being able; capacity to do or of doing something; having) / مَوْهِبَة (A skill or competence in doing; mental power; talent; aptitude.)  [ability]\nمثال: あなたは集中する力を失ってしまった。\n→ You've lost the ability to concentrate. / تَأْثِير, أَثَر (The result or outcome of a cause.)  [effect]\nمثال: チョコレートにはＬＤＬの酸化を防止する力がある。\n→ Chocolate acts to prevent LDL oxidisation. / جَهْد, جُهْد (The work involved in performing an activity; exertion.)  [effort]",
 "力こぶ": "ذَات اَلرَّأْسَيْن (Any muscle having two heads.) / ذَات اَلرَّأْسَيْن اَلْعَضُدِيَّة (The upper arm, especially the collective muscles of the upper arm.)  [(bulge of one's) biceps] / حَمَاس (fervour or devotion) / جُهْد (fervour or devotion)  [zeal]\nusu. as 〜を入れる",
 "力ずく": "قُوَّة (Ability to influence; strength or energy of body or mind; active power; vigour; ) / قُوَّة (Anything that is able to make a substantial change in a person or thing.) / أَجْبَرَ, اِضْطَرَّ (To compel (an adversary or partner) to trump a trick by leading a suit that he/s)  [(brute) force]\noft. as ～で\nمثال: 彼は群衆の中を力ずくで進んでいった。\n→ He muscled his way through the crowd.",
 "力づく": "قُوَّة (Ability to influence; strength or energy of body or mind; active power; vigour; ) / قُوَّة (Anything that is able to make a substantial change in a person or thing.) / أَجْبَرَ, اِضْطَرَّ (To compel (an adversary or partner) to trump a trick by leading a suit that he/s)  [(brute) force]\noft. as ～で\nمثال: 彼は群衆の中を力ずくで進んでいった。\n→ He muscled his way through the crowd.",
