 "即ち": "يَعْنِي, أَي (In other words; that is to say. Used to introduce a clarification or explanation)  [that is (to say)]\nمثال: 彼は非常に知識のある人、すなわち生き字引である。\n→ He is a man of great knowledge, that is to say, a walking dictionary. / بِدِقَّة (In a precise manner; exactly.)  [precisely] / آنَذَاكَ, حِينَئِذٍ (At that time.) / ثُمَّ (Soon afterward.) / ثُمَّ (Next in order of place.) / إِذًا, إِذَنْ (In that case.)  [then]\nas ...ば～; indicates that what follows is a natural consequence / فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [so]",
 "即今": "حَالِيًّا, فِي هٰذِهِ اَللَّحْظَة (At this moment; right now.)  [at the moment]",
